From: Vadim Deiss <letechnarb@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: report the tx rate that rate control chose

On an IPQ5018 AP with a QCN6122 5 GHz radio the station tx rate in
iw/LuCI shows 6 Mbit/s for HE stations while they are idle, and flips
between the real rate and 6 or 12 Mbit/s under load.

On chips that are not single_pdev_only the tx completions update
arsta->txrate only with extended tx stats enabled in debugfs, so the
HTT PPDU stats are the only source of the station tx rate, and
ath11k_update_per_peer_tx_stats() takes it from every PPDU. Many PPDUs
go out at a rate not chosen by rate control. Logging the PPDU stats
(NSS Wi-Fi offload, four HE stations) showed at CCK/OFDM rates: HE
sounding NDPAs (frame control 0x0054) at 6 Mbit/s, UL/MU trigger frames
(0x0024) at 6-24 Mbit/s, BARs, management frames, and ARP frames (QoS
data, 0x4288) that the firmware sends at 6 Mbit/s. Whichever comes last
is what userspace reports.

The firmware marks these PPDUs: bit 31 of the rate word of the user
rate TLV (skipped_rate_ctrl, valid when bit 30 is set) is set when the
rate did not come from rate control. Over about 75000 PPDUs it was
always valid, set on every CCK/OFDM PPDU and on a few non-data PPDUs at
HE rates, and clear on every HE data PPDU.

ath10k already uses its version of the same firmware flag for this
(9a9cf0e63f70 "ath10k: report tx rate using ieee80211_tx_rate_update()"):
"Firmware's rate control skips broadcast/management frames, if host has
configure fixed rates and in some other special cases." ath11k kept that
comment above the rate update, followed by a question, but never read
the flag.

Only let PPDUs whose rate came from rate control update arsta->txrate.
A fixed rate set through the bitrate mask also makes the firmware skip
rate control (seen with a single HE MCS), so record the rate code ath11k
sets with WMI_PEER_PARAM_FIXED_RATE on the peer it is set for, and the
one set with WMI_VDEV_PARAM_FIXED_RATE per vdev, and keep taking the
rate from PPDUs sent at that rate. Firmware that does not fill bit 30
keeps the old behaviour. The PPDU rate is now decoded into a local, so
last_txrate, the extended tx stats and ru_tones still describe every
PPDU as before; only the reported station rate is filtered.

Tested with four HE stations idle and under load, with a single fixed
HE MCS in the bitrate mask, and with a client forced to 802.11a, 11n
and 11ac: the reported rate follows rate control (legacy 36-54 Mbit/s,
HT MCS 15, VHT-MCS 5-7, HE-MCS 4-11) or shows the fixed HE MCS, and no
longer shows the basic-rate PPDUs. For the legacy client the firmware
left the flag clear on its data PPDUs. With the BSS switched to VHT160
and a single 24 Mbit/s legacy rate in the bitrate mask all stations
report 24 Mbit/s. Not tested: CCK rates and firmware without bit 30.

Filtering on the frame type, as mac80211 does for its own last_tx_rate
(c1ce5a74d113 "mac80211: Update last_tx_rate only for data frames") and
Qualcomm's datapath (qca-wifi-host-cmn) does for the peer tx rate, is
not enough here: the ARP frames are data, so an idle station would
still show 6 Mbit/s after every ARP broadcast.

The same symptom was fixed for chips without PPDU stats by taking the
rate from tx completions (1b8bb94c0612 "ath11k: report tx bitrate for
iw wlan station dump"); ath12k did the same for station mode
(8a9c06b40882 "wifi: ath12k: report station mode transmit rate").

Tested-on: QCN6122 hw1.0 AHB firmware 0x290b8862 (2024-09-23)

Signed-off-by: Vadim Deiss <letechnarb@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.h
@@ -1438,6 +1438,8 @@ enum HTT_PPDU_STATS_PPDU_TYPE {
 #define HTT_PPDU_STATS_USER_RATE_FLAGS_GI_M		GENMASK(27, 24)
 #define HTT_PPDU_STATS_USER_RATE_FLAGS_DCM_M		BIT(28)
 #define HTT_PPDU_STATS_USER_RATE_FLAGS_LDPC_M		BIT(29)
+#define HTT_PPDU_STATS_USER_RATE_FLAGS_SKIPPED_RC_VALID_M	BIT(30)
+#define HTT_PPDU_STATS_USER_RATE_FLAGS_SKIPPED_RC_M	BIT(31)
 
 #define HTT_USR_RATE_PREAMBLE(_val) \
 		FIELD_GET(HTT_PPDU_STATS_USER_RATE_FLAGS_PREAMBLE_M, _val)
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/peer.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/peer.h
@@ -91,6 +91,8 @@ struct ath11k_peer {
 	u16 sec_type;
 	u16 sec_type_grp;
 	bool is_authorized;
+	/* WMI_PEER_PARAM_FIXED_RATE code, protected by ab->base_lock */
+	u32 fixed_rate_code;
 	bool dp_setup_done;
 	struct ppdu_user_delayba ppdu_stats_delayba;
 	bool delayba_flag;
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.h
@@ -826,6 +826,8 @@ struct ath11k {
 	u32 num_started_vdevs;
 	u32 num_created_vdevs;
 	unsigned long long allocated_vdev_map;
+	/* WMI_VDEV_PARAM_FIXED_RATE code by vdev_id, protected by data_lock */
+	u32 vdev_fixed_rate_code[BITS_PER_LONG_LONG];
 
 	struct idr txmgmt_idr;
 	/* protects txmgmt_idr data */
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
@@ -4958,6 +4958,33 @@ ath11k_mac_bitrate_mask_num_he_rates(str
 	return num_rates;
 }
 
+static int ath11k_mac_set_peer_fixed_rate(struct ath11k_vif *arvif,
+					  struct ieee80211_sta *sta,
+					  u32 rate_code)
+{
+	struct ath11k *ar = arvif->ar;
+	struct ath11k_base *ab = ar->ab;
+	struct ath11k_peer *peer;
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = ath11k_wmi_set_peer_param(ar, sta->addr, arvif->vdev_id,
+					WMI_PEER_PARAM_FIXED_RATE, rate_code);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	/* The firmware does not run rate control for a peer with a fixed
+	 * rate. Record it on the peer the firmware applies it to, the PPDU
+	 * stats need it to tell the station data rate apart.
+	 */
+	spin_lock_bh(&ab->base_lock);
+	peer = ath11k_peer_find(ar, arvif->vdev_id, sta->addr);
+	if (peer)
+		peer->fixed_rate_code = rate_code;
+	spin_unlock_bh(&ab->base_lock);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static int
 ath11k_mac_set_peer_vht_fixed_rate(struct ath11k_vif *arvif,
 				   struct ieee80211_sta *sta,
@@ -4996,10 +5023,7 @@ ath11k_mac_set_peer_vht_fixed_rate(struc
 
 	rate_code = ATH11K_HW_RATE_CODE(vht_rate, nss - 1,
 					WMI_RATE_PREAMBLE_VHT);
-	ret = ath11k_wmi_set_peer_param(ar, sta->addr,
-					arvif->vdev_id,
-					WMI_PEER_PARAM_FIXED_RATE,
-					rate_code);
+	ret = ath11k_mac_set_peer_fixed_rate(arvif, sta, rate_code);
 	if (ret)
 		ath11k_warn(ar->ab,
 			    "failed to update STA %pM Fixed Rate %d: %d\n",
@@ -5047,10 +5071,7 @@ ath11k_mac_set_peer_he_fixed_rate(struct
 	rate_code = ATH11K_HW_RATE_CODE(he_rate, nss - 1,
 					WMI_RATE_PREAMBLE_HE);
 
-	ret = ath11k_wmi_set_peer_param(ar, sta->addr,
-					arvif->vdev_id,
-					WMI_PEER_PARAM_FIXED_RATE,
-					rate_code);
+	ret = ath11k_mac_set_peer_fixed_rate(arvif, sta, rate_code);
 	if (ret)
 		ath11k_warn(ar->ab,
 			    "failed to update sta %pM fixed rate %d: %d\n",
@@ -5095,10 +5116,7 @@ ath11k_mac_set_peer_ht_fixed_rate(struct
 
 	rate_code = ATH11K_HW_RATE_CODE(ht_rate, nss - 1,
 					WMI_RATE_PREAMBLE_HT);
-	ret = ath11k_wmi_set_peer_param(ar, sta->addr,
-					arvif->vdev_id,
-					WMI_PEER_PARAM_FIXED_RATE,
-					rate_code);
+	ret = ath11k_mac_set_peer_fixed_rate(arvif, sta, rate_code);
 	if (ret)
 		ath11k_warn(ar->ab,
 			    "failed to update STA %pM HT Fixed Rate %d: %d\n",
@@ -5396,10 +5414,8 @@ static void ath11k_sta_rc_update_wk(stru
 			 * the peer fixed rate settings as it has higher proprity
 			 * than peer assoc
 			 */
-			err = ath11k_wmi_set_peer_param(ar, sta->addr,
-							arvif->vdev_id,
-							WMI_PEER_PARAM_FIXED_RATE,
-							WMI_FIXED_RATE_NONE);
+			err = ath11k_mac_set_peer_fixed_rate(arvif, sta,
+							     WMI_FIXED_RATE_NONE);
 			if (err)
 				ath11k_warn(ar->ab,
 					    "failed to disable peer fixed rate for sta %pM: %d\n",
@@ -7675,6 +7691,9 @@ static int ath11k_mac_op_add_interface(s
 	ath11k_dbg(ab, ATH11K_DBG_MAC, "vdev %pM created, vdev_id %d\n",
 		   vif->addr, arvif->vdev_id);
 	ar->allocated_vdev_map |= 1LL << arvif->vdev_id;
+	spin_lock_bh(&ar->data_lock);
+	ar->vdev_fixed_rate_code[arvif->vdev_id] = 0;
+	spin_unlock_bh(&ar->data_lock);
 	ab->free_vdev_map &= ~(1LL << arvif->vdev_id);
 
 	spin_lock_bh(&ar->data_lock);
@@ -9478,6 +9497,10 @@ static int ath11k_mac_set_rate_params(st
 				    rate, ret);
 			return ret;
 		}
+
+		spin_lock_bh(&ar->data_lock);
+		ar->vdev_fixed_rate_code[arvif->vdev_id] = rate;
+		spin_unlock_bh(&ar->data_lock);
 	}
 
 	vdev_param = WMI_VDEV_PARAM_NSS;
@@ -9601,10 +9624,7 @@ static void ath11k_mac_disable_peer_fixe
 	struct ath11k *ar = arvif->ar;
 	int ret;
 
-	ret = ath11k_wmi_set_peer_param(ar, sta->addr,
-					arvif->vdev_id,
-					WMI_PEER_PARAM_FIXED_RATE,
-					WMI_FIXED_RATE_NONE);
+	ret = ath11k_mac_set_peer_fixed_rate(arvif, sta, WMI_FIXED_RATE_NONE);
 	if (ret)
 		ath11k_warn(ar->ab,
 			    "failed to disable peer fixed rate for STA %pM ret %d\n",
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
@@ -1674,6 +1674,33 @@ static int ath11k_htt_tlv_ppdu_soc_stats
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/* Whether the rate of a PPDU was chosen by rate control for the station,
+ * or is a fixed rate ath11k configured for it. The firmware flags PPDUs
+ * sent without rate control; firmware that does not fill the flag is
+ * trusted. Fixed rate codes always have the version bit set, so a zero
+ * or WMI_FIXED_RATE_NONE never matches.
+ */
+static bool ath11k_dp_rx_ppdu_rate_chosen(struct ath11k *ar,
+					  struct ath11k_peer *peer,
+					  u32 rate_flags, u8 preamble,
+					  u8 mcs, u8 nss)
+{
+	u32 rate_code;
+
+	if (!(rate_flags & HTT_PPDU_STATS_USER_RATE_FLAGS_SKIPPED_RC_VALID_M) ||
+	    !(rate_flags & HTT_PPDU_STATS_USER_RATE_FLAGS_SKIPPED_RC_M))
+		return true;
+
+	if (preamble == WMI_RATE_PREAMBLE_CCK)
+		mcs &= ~ATH11k_HW_RATECODE_CCK_SHORT_PREAM_MASK;
+
+	rate_code = ATH11K_HW_RATE_CODE(mcs, nss - 1, preamble);
+
+	return rate_code == peer->fixed_rate_code ||
+	       (peer->vdev_id < ARRAY_SIZE(ar->vdev_fixed_rate_code) &&
+		rate_code == ar->vdev_fixed_rate_code[peer->vdev_id]);
+}
+
 static void
 ath11k_update_per_peer_tx_stats(struct ath11k *ar,
 				struct htt_ppdu_stats *ppdu_stats, u8 user)
@@ -1693,6 +1720,7 @@ ath11k_update_per_peer_tx_stats(struct a
 	u32 tx_duration = 0;
 	u8 tid = HTT_PPDU_STATS_NON_QOS_TID;
 	bool is_ampdu = false;
+	struct rate_info txrate;
 
 	if (!(usr_stats->tlv_flags & BIT(HTT_PPDU_STATS_TAG_USR_RATE)))
 		return;
@@ -1729,11 +1757,6 @@ ath11k_update_per_peer_tx_stats(struct a
 	ru_start = user_rate->ru_start;
 	ru_tone = user_rate->ru_end;
 
-	/* Note: If host configured fixed rates and in some other special
-	 * cases, the broadcast/management frames are sent in different rates.
-	 * Firmware rate's control to be skipped for this?
-	 */
-
 	if (flags == WMI_RATE_PREAMBLE_HE && mcs > ATH11K_HE_MCS_MAX) {
 		ath11k_warn(ab, "Invalid HE mcs %d peer stats",  mcs);
 		return;
@@ -1772,43 +1795,54 @@ ath11k_update_per_peer_tx_stats(struct a
 	sta = peer->sta;
 	arsta = ath11k_sta_to_arsta(sta);
 
-	memset(&arsta->txrate, 0, sizeof(arsta->txrate));
+	memset(&txrate, 0, sizeof(txrate));
 
 	switch (flags) {
 	case WMI_RATE_PREAMBLE_OFDM:
-		arsta->txrate.legacy = rate;
+		txrate.legacy = rate;
 		break;
 	case WMI_RATE_PREAMBLE_CCK:
-		arsta->txrate.legacy = rate;
+		txrate.legacy = rate;
 		break;
 	case WMI_RATE_PREAMBLE_HT:
-		arsta->txrate.mcs = mcs + 8 * (nss - 1);
-		arsta->txrate.flags = RATE_INFO_FLAGS_MCS;
+		txrate.mcs = mcs + 8 * (nss - 1);
+		txrate.flags = RATE_INFO_FLAGS_MCS;
 		if (sgi)
-			arsta->txrate.flags |= RATE_INFO_FLAGS_SHORT_GI;
+			txrate.flags |= RATE_INFO_FLAGS_SHORT_GI;
 		break;
 	case WMI_RATE_PREAMBLE_VHT:
-		arsta->txrate.mcs = mcs;
-		arsta->txrate.flags = RATE_INFO_FLAGS_VHT_MCS;
+		txrate.mcs = mcs;
+		txrate.flags = RATE_INFO_FLAGS_VHT_MCS;
 		if (sgi)
-			arsta->txrate.flags |= RATE_INFO_FLAGS_SHORT_GI;
+			txrate.flags |= RATE_INFO_FLAGS_SHORT_GI;
 		break;
 	case WMI_RATE_PREAMBLE_HE:
-		arsta->txrate.mcs = mcs;
-		arsta->txrate.flags = RATE_INFO_FLAGS_HE_MCS;
-		arsta->txrate.he_dcm = dcm;
-		arsta->txrate.he_gi = ath11k_mac_he_gi_to_nl80211_he_gi(sgi);
-		arsta->txrate.he_ru_alloc = ath11k_mac_phy_he_ru_to_nl80211_he_ru_alloc
+		txrate.mcs = mcs;
+		txrate.flags = RATE_INFO_FLAGS_HE_MCS;
+		txrate.he_dcm = dcm;
+		txrate.he_gi = ath11k_mac_he_gi_to_nl80211_he_gi(sgi);
+		txrate.he_ru_alloc = ath11k_mac_phy_he_ru_to_nl80211_he_ru_alloc
 						((user_rate->ru_end -
 						 user_rate->ru_start) + 1);
 		break;
 	}
 
-	arsta->txrate.nss = nss;
+	txrate.nss = nss;
+
+	txrate.bw = ath11k_mac_bw_to_mac80211_bw(bw);
+
+	/* Sounding NDPAs, trigger, management and some data frames (ARP) go
+	 * out at a rate not chosen by rate control, typically 6 Mbit/s.
+	 * These PPDU stats are the only source of the station tx rate unless
+	 * the tx completions report it (extended tx stats or
+	 * single_pdev_only), so do not let such a PPDU replace it.
+	 */
+	if (ath11k_dp_rx_ppdu_rate_chosen(ar, peer, user_rate->rate_flags,
+					  flags, mcs, nss))
+		arsta->txrate = txrate;
 
-	arsta->txrate.bw = ath11k_mac_bw_to_mac80211_bw(bw);
 	arsta->tx_duration += tx_duration;
-	memcpy(&arsta->last_txrate, &arsta->txrate, sizeof(struct rate_info));
+	memcpy(&arsta->last_txrate, &txrate, sizeof(struct rate_info));
 
 	/* PPDU stats reported for mgmt packet doesn't have valid tx bytes.
 	 * So skip peer stats update for mgmt packets.
@@ -1827,10 +1861,11 @@ ath11k_update_per_peer_tx_stats(struct a
 		peer_stats->ru_start = ru_start;
 		peer_stats->mu_grpid = mu_grpid;
 		peer_stats->mu_pos   = mu_pos;
-		peer_stats->ru_tones = arsta->txrate.he_ru_alloc;
+		peer_stats->ru_tones = txrate.he_ru_alloc;
 
 		if (ath11k_debugfs_is_extd_tx_stats_enabled(ar))
-			ath11k_debugfs_sta_add_tx_stats(arsta, peer_stats, rate_idx);
+			ath11k_debugfs_sta_add_tx_stats(arsta, &txrate, peer_stats,
+							rate_idx);
 	}
 
 	usr_stats->rate_stats_updated = true;
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/debugfs_sta.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/debugfs_sta.h
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@
 void ath11k_debugfs_sta_op_add(struct ieee80211_hw *hw, struct ieee80211_vif *vif,
 			       struct ieee80211_sta *sta, struct dentry *dir);
 void ath11k_debugfs_sta_add_tx_stats(struct ath11k_sta *arsta,
